                "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 4 at 9:10PM MDT until September 5 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of central New Mexico, including the following\narea, South Central Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Saturday morning through Saturday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Thunderstorms will develop over the higher terrain late Saturday\nmorning then drift erratically into the nearby lower terrain\nthrough Saturday afternoon. Rainfall rates in excess of 2 inches\nan hour will result in a higher risk for flash flooding on the\nRuidoso area burn scars. The flash flood risk will taper off by\nlate afternoon.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
